00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:25.300
prices are not fixed engineering outcomes but adjustable levers that respond to policy shifts in real

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:31.820
time. This adjustment matters because it alters the demand signal that reaches the factory. A higher

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:38.220
posted price can reduce volume even when the subsidized net price stays similar, which in turn affects

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:44.320
production planning and supplier contracts. In markets where subsidies are temporary or subject to

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:50.720
annual resets, manufacturers that treat the incentive as permanent risk building capacity that later

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:57.880
proves mismatched to unsubsidized demand. Registration gains across multiple European markets are feeding

